# author-geo ownership boundary — see THEMING.md for the full explanation.
#
# This repo splits into an UPSTREAM (engine) zone and an IMPLEMENTER-owned
# (theming + content) zone, so `git pull upstream main` stays conflict-free.
#
# Implementer-owned — edit these freely, upstream never touches them:
#   src/overrides/**              selective component/layout shadows (@theme
#                                  alias) PLUS the free-form CSS override slot
#                                  at src/overrides/styles/site.css (the
#                                  @theme-styles/site.css virtual specifier,
#                                  see vite-plugins/theme-styles-override.mjs)
#   src/styles/theme.css          re-theming tokens (colors/fonts/spacing)
#   src/content/**                your books/series/author/hubs/events content
#   src/config.ts                 author-editable site config (theme mode, nav, ...)
#
# Upstream-owned — do not edit; pull updates via `git pull upstream main`:
#   everything else in src/, in particular:
#   src/lib/jsonld.ts       the structured-data engine (Tier 3 — never
#                           overridable, see THEMING.md)
#   src/pages/**            page routes (Tier 3 — never overridable)
#   src/styles/base.css     upstream structural/layout CSS
#   src/components/**, src/layouts/**  — the ORIGINALS; to change one, copy
#                           it into src/overrides/ at the same relative path
#                           (Tier 2) rather than editing it in place here.
#
# merge=union on theme.css: a theme.css change is almost always independent
# per-line token edits (colors/fonts/spacing), so letting git keep BOTH
# sides' lines on a pull conflict (rather than conflict-marking) is a safe,
# low-risk convenience for this one specific, narrowly-scoped file. Nothing
# else in the repo gets this treatment — a union merge on real code could
# silently splice together two incompatible versions of the same logic, so
# it is deliberately not applied anywhere else.
src/styles/theme.css merge=union
